			"16": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "STRING\n\nText is handled by the string type.\nThere are two important nodes you should know about when working with strings.\n\nThe String In node will take a string from the user.\nThis is ideal for when you want to create a custom text source.\n\nThe String node is often used to convert other data types to strings.\nThis node is also capable of producing strings on its own.\nIn the second example we convert the X and Y values to strings so we can display them on the screen. We also use a String node to wire \"X\/Y:\""
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 957.91455078125,
					"width": 1194.0830078125,
					"x": 432,
					"y": 366.246368408203125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Group",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"17": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TEXT RENDER\n\nSurprise! There is another super important node to know when dealing with text.\nThe Text Render node is used to convert strings to textures.\nThis is the node that you use to get the strings onto the screen.\n\nThe node has a LOT of parameters, but they are all very straightforward for anyone who has ever used a text editor.\n\nThe node is also capable of generating glows and outlines.\nThese parameters are hidden by default but can be tweaked either in the node panel or by making the parameter visible.\n\nThe font and style are set in the node panel.\n\nAssignment: expand the patch below so that the text has a pulsating glowing outline in the Impact font. Make sure you write something cheeky!"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 957.91455078125,
					"width": 1194.0830078125,
					"x": 1664.5859375,
					"y": 366.246368408203125
