						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "CONCATENATE\n\nWire has a bunch of tools to edit text, most of which we will cover in the advanced text tutorial.\nThere are however two tools that we do not want to keep from you: Concatenate and Change Case.\nLet's start with Concatenate.\n\nString concatenation is a very nerdy way to say: combine multiple lines of text.\nThe Concatenate node takes two or more strings and combines them with a given separator.\nYou've already seen the Concatenate node in action in the example above where it was used to combine the X and Y string with the \"X\/Y: \" string.\nThe amount of inputs can be set in the node panel.\n\nAssignment: create 4 string nodes and concatenate them."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 957.91455078125,
					"width": 1194.0830078125,
					"x": 432.320587158203125,
